# HOK-1320: Wavemill should attempt to resolve readiness failures

The ready check correctly detected a problem with PR 318 and it failed the readiness check. But instead of burping the JSON into the log output we should alert the LLM about the failure and allow it to attempt to fix the issue. 

This will require figuring out whether the LLM is still active and prompting the appropriate information to them. We should allow the user to configure the number of re-tries the llm gets before the readiness check fails - I'd assume three as a default. 

